## What
Given a map of cell → its dependencies, produce a topological ordering so cells are recalculated in the right order (dependencies before dependents).

## File: include/dep_graph.h + src/dep_graph.cpp
```cpp
#pragma once
#include "cell_address.h"
#include <unordered_map>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <vector>

class DepGraph {
public:
    // Record that `cell` depends on `dependency`
    void add_dependency(const CellAddress& cell, const CellAddress& dependency);

    // Remove all dependencies for a cell (call before re-parsing its formula)
    void remove_cell(const CellAddress& cell);

    // Returns cells in evaluation order (dependencies before dependents)
    // Returns empty if a cycle is detected
    std::vector<CellAddress> topo_sort() const;

    bool has_cycle() const;

private:
    // adjacency: cell -> set of cells it depends on
    std::unordered_map<CellAddress, std::unordered_set<CellAddress>> deps_;
};
```

## Algorithm
Use DFS-based topological sort (Kahn's algorithm or recursive DFS with a "visited" set and a "in-stack" set for cycle detection).

## Acceptance criteria
- A → B → C sorts as [C, B, A] (C evaluated first, then B uses C, then A uses B)
- A graph with no dependencies sorts in any valid order

